@startuml
title Aztec Connect June 2026: settlement loop bound not covered by the proof
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FDEEEE
  BorderColor #B54A4A
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF8F8
  DiamondBorderColor #B54A4A
  ArrowColor #4A2020
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF8F8
  BorderColor #B54A4A
}

start
:attacker builds a rollup block
with 32 transaction slots;<<#EAF6F0>>
:slot 1 = noop, slots 2 to 32 =
fabricated deposit rows;
:set numRealTxs = 1 in the calldata;
note right
  numRealTxs is read from calldata
  and is not a public input
  constrained by the circuit
end note

fork
  :circuit hashes all 32 slots
  with the SHA-256 precompile;<<#EAF6F0>>
  :zk proof is valid for the
  full 32-slot block;<<#EAF6F0>>
fork again
  :RollupProcessorV3.processRollup()
  iterates i in [0, numRealTxs);
  :loop stops after slot 1;
  :deposit rows in slots 2 to 32
  are never settled on L1;
end fork

:proof verifies, block is accepted;
:L2 balances credited for deposits
that L1 never processed;

if (attacker withdraws?) then (yes)
  :submit an honest withdrawal proof
  against the unbacked L2 balance;
  :bridge pays out real L1 assets;
  stop
else (no)
  stop
endif
@enduml
